Privacy
I Privacy is one of the fundamental right of individuals: I Universal Declaration of the Human Rights at the assembly of the United Nations (Article 12), 1948. I European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), voted in 2016 will become effective in 2018. I One of the main challenge of the “Information Society”.
I Risk: collect and use of digital traces and personal data for fraudulent purposes. I Examples: targeted spam, identity theft, profiling, (unfair) discrimination (to be discussed later).
