 Introduction Privacy Transparency, accountability and fairness
De-anonymization attack
I De-anonymization attack : the adversary takes as input a sanitized dataset and some background knowledge and tries to infer the identities of the individuals contained in the dataset. I Specific form of inference attack. I Example : Sweeney’s original de-anonymization attack via linking.
I The re-identification risk measures the success probability of this attack.
