Opacity of machine learning algorithms
I Machine learning has a central role in most of the personalized systems.
I Opacity: difficulty of understanding and explaining their decision due to their complex design.
I Example: the classifier outputted by a deep learning algorithm is typically composed of many layers of neural networks.
I Risk of “algorithmic dictatorship” (Rouvroy): loss of control of individuals on their digital lives due to automated decision if there is no remediation procedure.
